    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 18,
    "summary": "King Lamoni supposes that Ammon is the Great Spirit—Ammon teaches the king about the Creation, God’s dealings with men, and the redemption that comes through Christ—Lamoni believes and falls to the earth as if dead. About 90 B.C.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
