        "reference": "Alma 18:2",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And they answered the king, and said: Whether he be the Great Spirit or a man, we know not; but this much we do know, that he cannot be slain by the enemies of the king; neither can they scatter the king’s flocks when he is with us, because of his expertness and great strength; therefore, we know that he is a friend to the king. And now, O king, we do not believe that a man has such great power, for we know he cannot be slain.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 132,
            "text": "Alma 17:36 (34–38)."
